.TH HARDPOINT\-SERVER 6 "2026" "Hardpoint" "Games"
.SH NAME
hardpoint\-server \- dedicated server for Hardpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hardpoint\-server
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the same authoritative server the game hosts internally, with no window,
no renderer and no audio. It holds the simulation, validates every client
action, fills empty slots with bots, cycles maps at the end of each match and
answers local network discovery so it appears in the in-game server browser.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
UDP port to listen on. Default 27015.
.TP
.BI \-\-map " NAME"
Starting map: IRONVEIL, STORMWORKS, BELVOIR, GREENLINE, WHITEOUT, HIGHRISE,
DRYDOCK, FOUNDRY, SALTBITE, DEEPWELL, JUNCTION or OVERPASS.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " NAME"
TDM, FFA, DOM, S&D or GUN.
.TP
.BI \-\-bots " n"
Bots to fill the server with.
.TP
.BI \-\-skill " 0\-3"
Bot difficulty: recruit, regular, veteran, elite.
.TP
.BI \-\-players " n"
Maximum players, including bots.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " text"
Server name shown in the browser.
.TP
.BI \-\-password " text"
Require a password to join.
.TP
.BI \-\-tracker " address"
Register with a tracker so the server is listed off the local network.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH SERVICE
The package installs a systemd unit reading
.IR /etc/hardpoint/server.conf .
.PP
.RS
systemctl enable \-\-now hardpoint\-server
.RE
.PP
The unit runs under a dynamic user with no filesystem access and a UDP socket
as its only capability.
.SH SECURITY
Clients are never trusted. Positions, damage, kills, score, match state,
respawns and unlocks are all decided by the server, and every command is
bounds\-checked and rate\-limited before it is applied.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hardpoint (6)
